{
  "_comment": [
    "Report 1044 — 'Total test as STAT with ACCEPTANCE' (ASH Reports2).",
    "Captured from the portal's own GetReportData request, unchanged apart from",
    "the two dates and loginUserId, which the server fills in per request.",
    "Joined onto the samples received by SAMPLE_NO: it carries the sorting and",
    "result-entry stamps the received report has no column for, so a sample's",
    "turnaround past acceptance can be read off the same row.",
    "CATEGORYNAME is left at '%' and SITE at All. SERVICENAME is not: asked",
    "across every service the report outruns its own SQL, so test_filter has it",
    "asked one service at a time, for the test names the samples received",
    "report brought back over the same span.",
    "It has a row per test, so match_column pairs its TEST_NAME with the main",
    "report's: without that, one test's stamps would land on all of them.",
    "Re-capture it the same way if the HIS ever changes the report's filters."
  ],
  "_meta": {
    "title": "STAT tests with acceptance",
    "key_column": "SAMPLE_NO",
    "date_filters": {
      "from": "FROM_DATE",
      "to": "TO_DATE"
    },
    "test_filter": {
      "filter": "SERVICENAME",
      "all": "%"
    },
    "match_column": {
      "linked": "TEST_NAME",
      "main": "TEST_NAME"
    }
  },
